WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
ModelCheck reviews binary-classification experiment exports.
This walkthrough uses synthetic samples.

00:04.000 --> 00:10.500
The sample inspection calculates metrics through MCP tools.
No model request is needed for these calculations.

00:10.500 --> 00:18.000
Candidate accuracy is 85%, versus a 90% baseline.
Web recall falls from 90% to 50%; studio recall rises to 100%.

00:18.000 --> 00:21.500
Load the recorded AI review.
This replays an earlier v1 result without sending a model request.

00:21.500 --> 00:29.000
The review is labeled “Recorded AI review · v1”.
Its findings cite measured tool evidence.

00:29.000 --> 00:35.500
Prediction exports cannot prove the test set was never used for tuning.
The interface flags that unsupported claim in the original response.

00:35.500 --> 00:43.500
Draft a manual follow-up experiment.
Choose changes on validation data and keep the test set held out.

00:43.500 --> 00:50.000
Review the exact specification and approval digest.
Nothing is saved until approval.

00:50.000 --> 00:56.500
Approve the specification.
The application saves exactly one experiment JSON file.

00:56.500 --> 01:11.500
Download the approved experiment JSON.
This is a replay-and-approval demo, not a new live v2 evaluation.
